    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-09105 is refunded in full to the rider, and no compensation is payable to the driver.\n\nWhy the fee does not stand. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-09105) places him stationary at 219.77 m from the Tower B pickup pin for the entire record — 34 fixes from 13:05:00 to 13:10:30, speed 0.0 kph, trace distance 0.0 km, and zero fixes inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius (qualifying_fix_count 0, longest qualifying run 0.0 s). Under POL-NS-02 the driver is not deemed to have ARRIVED at the pickup point, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails and the fee is not chargeable. This is a wrong-entrance arrival governed by POL-NS-03: the driver was stationary outside the arrival radius but inside the 400 m ceiling (219.77 m), and held that position for 330 seconds, longer than the 300-second LARGE_VENUE dwell, so POL-NS-03 refunds the cancellation fee in full. Independently, the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 300-second minimum — a 300-second shortfall — which under POL-NS-06 also makes the fee non-chargeable whether or not the rider was present.\n\nFault lies with the driver, so no compensation. The chat log (EV-CHAT-09105) shows the rider naming the sub-location — 'I am at Tower B ride-hail pickup' at 13:05:05 and 'That is the other entrance. Please come to Tower B.' at 13:06:35 — while the driver replied only that he was 'waiting at the mall taxi stand' at 13:06:00 and never moved before cancelling at 13:10:30. The driver's own filed statement concedes he 'did not move to Tower B'. Under POL-NS-03(i) the driver bears the loss and receives no compensation, so the POL-NS-07 payment of 80% (SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00) is not payable. The driver-side claim that this is a wrong-face-of-same-venue case is accepted, but it leads to the same result: the fee is refunded and, because the rider specified the tower, limb (ii)'s pin-ambiguity goodwill of SGD 2.00 does not apply either.\n\nThe arrival marker is not false. At the 13:05:20 marker the driver was 219.77 m from the pin — inside POL-NS-05's 300 m trigger — and at 0.0 kph, below its 15 kph trigger, so POL-NS-05 does not engage at all; POL-NS-05 expressly sends a driver stationary within 300 m but outside the arrival radius to POL-NS-03. No false-arrival referral under POL-NS-05(ii) is entered against the driver. The rider's POL-NS-04 argument reaches the same outcome (full refund, no compensation) and changes nothing; on its own terms it is also doubtful, since the driver replied at 13:06:00 to the rider's 13:05:05 locating message, inside the 120-second window.\n\nAmount. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-09105) itemises the cancellation fee as the only chargeable line — base_fare 0.00, platform_fee 0.00, waiting_time_fee 0.00, tolls 0.00, total_charged SGD 4.00, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00. SGD 4.00 is also the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) under fee_schedule.resolution_rule, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect, and the full refund is SGD 4.00.\n\nIntegrity and escalation. The trace has 100% coverage, 34 fixes, no gaps and rider_track present; the chat log holds 4 messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count; the arrived 13:05:20 event matches the trace cadence. No limb of POL-NS-08 is engaged, no two artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, and no POL-NS-09 trigger fires (the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check is not in play because the fee itself does not stand). Confidence is above the 0.70 floor. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09105-01 is MISSING (no payload, weight 0.0) and its absence cannot be used to sum separate in-geofence intervals under POL-NS-06(i); it carries nothing and does not affect the outcome."
  },
